## Feature Breakdown (55 Total)

### 1. Volatility Features (12) - **CRITICAL**

| Feature | Description | Why Important |
|---------|-------------|---------------|
| Rolling Vol (5-min) | Short-term volatility | Immediate regime detection |
| Rolling Vol (15-min) | Medium-term volatility | Trend confirmation |
| Rolling Vol (30-min) | Longer-term volatility | Regime stability |
| Rolling Vol (60-min) | Hourly volatility | Intraday pattern |
| Parkinson Vol | High-low based estimator | More efficient than close-to-close |
| Garman-Klass Vol | OHLC-based estimator | Most efficient estimator |
| Vol Percentile | Current vs historical | Regime identification |
| Vol of Vol | Volatility stability | Regime change detection |
| Vol Trend | Increasing/decreasing | Directional bias |
| IV vs Realized Spread | Premium/discount | Strategy selection |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Your Insight is Correct**: High volatility → Long straddle profitable; Low volatility → Short straddle profitable. These 12 features enable the model to identify volatility regimes accurately.

### 2. Price & Returns (10)

- Close (normalized by day open)
- Returns: 1-min, 5-min, 15-min, 30-min
- VWAP distance
- Distance from day high/low
- Price momentum

### 3. Greeks (10) - Using Black-Scholes

**Individual Greeks**:
- Delta (CE & PE)
- Gamma, Vega, Theta
- Vanna, Volga (second-order for volatility sensitivity)

**Position Greeks**:
- Net Delta exposure
- Gamma exposure
- Vega exposure

### 4. Technical Indicators (6)

- RSI (14-period)
- MACD (line, signal, histogram)
- Bollinger Band position
- ATR (Average True Range)

### 5. Position Features (10)

- CE/PE lots (normalized)
- CE/PE ratio
- Premium deployed (absolute & % of capital)
- Strike distances from current price
- Entry prices
- Unrealized PnL

### 6. Time Features (4)

- Minutes since market open
- Minutes to market close
- Sine/Cosine encoding (cyclical time)

### 7. Risk Metrics (3)

- Current drawdown
- Max drawdown
- Rolling Sharpe ratio

