## How Features Are Calculated (NO Simulated Data)

### Example: Volatility Features

```python
# From your real close prices
closes = [21500, 21505, 21512, 21508, ...]  # Real data from CSV

# Rolling volatility (30-min window)
returns = np.diff(closes) / closes[:-1]
vol_30min = np.std(returns[-30:]) * np.sqrt(252 * 390)

# Parkinson volatility (from real high/low)
highs = [21510, 21515, 21520, ...]  # Real data
lows = [21495, 21500, 21505, ...]   # Real data
hl_ratio = np.log(highs / lows)
parkinson_vol = np.sqrt(np.sum(hl_ratio**2) / (4*np.log(2)*n))
```

### Example: Greeks (Black-Scholes)

```python
# Using real underlying price from your data
S = 21505  # Current close price from CSV
K = 21500  # Strike (set at position entry)
T = minutes_to_close / (252 * 390)  # Real time from datetime
r = 0.06   # config.RISK_FREE_RATE
σ = 0.15   # config.IV_ESTIMATE

# Black-Scholes calculation
d1 = (np.log(S/K) + (r + 0.5*σ²)*T) / (σ*√T)
delta = N(d1)  # Normal CDF
gamma = N'(d1) / (S * σ * √T)
vanna = vega * (1 - d1/(σ*√T))
```

**Everything uses real data** - no simulation!

